c-stack: fix SIGSTKSZ preprocessor use on modern glibc hosts

glibc >= 2.34 turned SIGSTKSZ into a sysconf()-based function call
instead of a compile-time constant, which breaks the
"#elif HAVE_LIBSIGSEGV && SIGSTKSZ < 16384" preprocessor arithmetic
in this bundled gnulib c-stack.c -- a syntax error, not just a value
change, since the macro no longer expands to an integer literal.

Real error hit building host-m4 1.4.18 on this dev machine (glibc
2.36, Debian 12):

    c-stack.c:55:26: error: missing binary operator before token "("

This only affects the HOST build (m4 is a host-side autotools/build
dependency here, never shipped to the ARM target). The libsigsegv
2.6-2.8 workaround the elif branch existed for is irrelevant for this
use -- just force the same safe fixed stack size unconditionally.

Same class of problem as this package's existing (upstream Buildroot)
0001/0002-fflush-*.patch (glibc ABI-detail removal breaking old
gnulib code on a newer host glibc than this 2019-era Buildroot tree
was ever tested against). Kept as a global-patch-dir addition rather
than editing the vendored buildroot/package/m4/ patches directly, so
the vendored Buildroot tree stays untouched -- same convention as the
fakeroot _STAT_VER patch.

--- a/lib/c-stack.c
+++ b/lib/c-stack.c
@@ -50,15 +50,13 @@
 #if ! HAVE_STACK_T && ! defined stack_t
 typedef struct sigaltstack stack_t;
 #endif
-#ifndef SIGSTKSZ
-# define SIGSTKSZ 16384
-#elif HAVE_LIBSIGSEGV && SIGSTKSZ < 16384
-/* libsigsegv 2.6 through 2.8 have a bug where some architectures use
-   more than the Linux default of an 8k alternate stack when deciding
-   if a fault was caused by stack overflow.  */
-# undef SIGSTKSZ
-# define SIGSTKSZ 16384
-#endif
+/* glibc >= 2.34 turned SIGSTKSZ into a sysconf()-based function call,
+   not a compile-time constant, which breaks the "#elif SIGSTKSZ < N"
+   preprocessor arithmetic below on a modern host. This host-only
+   build tool doesn't need the old libsigsegv 2.6-2.8 workaround the
+   elif branch existed for -- just force a safe fixed size. */
+#undef SIGSTKSZ
+#define SIGSTKSZ 16384

 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
